/-! ## Section 9.4 application, Hadamard matrix growth lower bound

Higham, 2nd ed., section 9.4 (printed p. 170): a Hadamard matrix `H_n` has
entries `±1` with mutually orthogonal rows, so `H_n H_nᵀ = n I` and
`H_n⁻¹ = n⁻¹ H_nᵀ`.  Applying Theorem 9.8 with `α = max|h_{ij}| = 1` and
`β = max|(H_n⁻¹)_{ij}| = 1/n` gives `θ = (αβ)⁻¹ = n`, hence the growth factor
for GE without pivoting satisfies `ρ_n ≥ n`.  This is the third of the three
section-9.4 illustrations of Theorem 9.8 (the sine matrix `S_n`, eq. (9.12),
and the Fourier/Vandermonde matrix `V_n`, eq. (9.13), are formalized below and
above respectively).  We state it for any real matrix satisfying the Hadamard
identities; existence of Hadamard matrices for a given `n` is a separate
combinatorial fact and is not asserted here. -/













